Put your processor code here.

This directory MUST contain a file named "Dockerfile". The pipeline builds
./code/Dockerfile to produce the processor image.

*** BASE IMAGE CONSTRAINT (read before you write the Dockerfile) ***
Your Dockerfile `FROM` MUST be a PUBLIC image (Docker Hub, quay.io, ghcr.io, ...).
The build runs in a public pipeline that CANNOT be given private-registry
credentials (there is nowhere safe to put them), so a private base image will fail
at build time with a login/pull 401.

*** SECURITY SCAN GATE ***
The built image is scanned (Grype + Trivy); HIGH/CRITICAL vulnerabilities BLOCK
publishing, and most come from the base image. Pick a slim, freshly patched base
(...-slim, alpine, distroless) and keep build tools out of the final image
(multi-stage build).

The Dockerfile ENTRYPOINT/baseCommand must match the "baseCommand" in the
.cwl file at the repo root.

Delete this placeholder once you have added your Dockerfile.
